## 9. SHORT ORDER NUMBERS

Generate short customer-facing order numbers, such as:

024, 025, 026, 027.

The visible counter resets every 48 hours from the configured cycle start time, using Asia/Kolkata as the timezone.

Requirements:
- Generate numbers on the server.
- Use an atomic database counter or transaction.
- Prevent duplicate numbers within the same location and cycle.
- Store a permanent internal order UUID.
- Store the order cycle identifier.
- Preserve existing order numbers after a reset.
- Never reassign numbers to outstanding orders.
- Support concurrent orders safely.

The short number may be reused in a later cycle, so staff must be able to distinguish orders using the location, cycle, timestamp, and other appropriate details.

