## 33. DEFINITION OF DONE

The first working release must support this complete workflow:

1. Owner signs in.
2. Owner selects the restaurant or dhaba.
3. Owner creates menu categories and dishes.
4. Owner configures table QR codes and UPI QR.
5. Customer opens the website or scans a table QR.
6. Customer adds food to the cart.
7. Customer submits an order.
8. Server creates a permanent order ID and a short display number.
9. Customer receives a digital bill and screenshot reminder.
10. Kitchen tablet receives the order.
11. Kitchen plays a bell after sound is enabled.
12. Staff prepare the food.
13. Cashier views the order and payment status.
14. Cashier verifies and records cash or UPI payment.
15. Kitchen marks the order READY.
16. The number appears on the collection TV.
17. Staff mark the order COLLECTED.
18. The number disappears from the active collection list.
19. Admin can review the order, payment record, and status history.
20. Inventory records stock entries, recipes, consumption, imports, and estimated stock duration.

Begin by examining the available development environment and implementing the first functional release. Continue in manageable stages without abandoning the shared architecture.

At the end of each stage, state what actually works, what has been tested, and what still requires configuration. Never claim an unfinished feature is complete.